desc:GFX Lab G HPT77 [synth]
//tags: instrument synth formant voice drone cinematic
//author: JGWizrad / Garden FX (GFX)
// Requires gfx-lab-drift, gfx-lab-output, gfx-lab-uimin, gfx-lab-bverb (.jsfx-inc) in the same folder.
//
// HPT77 - a cinematic texture instrument in the spirit of deep alien vocalisations, monolithic low fog horns and
// alien rhythmic pulses. Every sound is synthesised.
//
// SIGNAL FLOW
//   VOICE (per key, 16 voices): a glottal buzz at the key's pitch with a growl an octave below and a breath of air,
//   through four formant resonators that glide from vowel to vowel in an unknown language (each voice its own
//   sequence of "syllables", a soft consonant click at each). FORMANT SHIFT moves every formant +/-12 semitones
//   (down = a vast throat, up = smaller, stranger).
//   GROUPS: BASS, TENOR, ALTO and SOPRANO sing together (each key sounds every group that is ON) - each with its own
//   sung-vowel formants (the growl fades out and the breath grows a little in the higher voices), level-matched in its
//   own range. Each group's key (in its colour: bass blue, tenor green, alto orange, soprano rose) switches it on and
//   off (lit = singing); EDIT (top bar) opens the LAYERS (the last one looked at) and closes them. Each group's LAYER:
//   AMP ENVELOPE (ATTACK, DECAY, SUSTAIN, RELEASE; under the pattern each syllable starts its own envelope, STACCATO
//   clips it), FILTER ENVELOPE (the same four, its own; it starts with the amp's), FILTER (MODE: LP 12, LP 24, BP, HP;
//   CUTOFF, RESONANCE, ENV AMOUNT +/-6 octaves, KEY TRACK), GROUP (LEVEL, OCTAVE -2 .. +2). The title lamp switches the
//   group on and off too; the tabs move between the layers, CLOSE (or EDIT) returns to the panel.
//   Levels and cut-offs glide (60 ms); a MODE change dips for 5 ms. Wide open (LP, CUTOFF at the top, no ENV, no KEY
//   TRACK) the filter is skipped. GROWL, SYLLABLE (time) and VELOCITY sit under the big knobs.
//   FILTER LFO (in the FILTER section): a sine on the cut-off, +/-4 octaves, locked to the tempo (4 bars .. 1/32).
//   STEP SEQUENCER (in each layer, Oontecho's): its lamp switches it in; 8 - 32 steps of 1/4 .. 1/32, each a LEVEL
//   (a bar - drag across them to draw, right-drag to erase) and an ACCENT (the row under them: click or drag). The
//   pattern moves the group's volume (DEPTH), its place in the stereo field (PAN: odd steps one way, even the other,
//   as far as the step's level) and its cut-off (FILTER: up to 5 octaves up or down at full level); accented steps are
//   louder (ACCENT: up to +6 dB) and open the filter (up to 1.5 octaves). GLIDE: from a fast, click-free edge to a
//   soft swell; SWING delays every second step. The arrows rotate the pattern, RND makes one, FILL sets every step
//   full. It runs with REAPER's grid while it plays and on at the project tempo while it is stopped; each group has
//   its own pattern (saved with the project).
//   FOG HORN (one, for the whole instrument): two reedy low tones at FOG TUNE, FOG DETUNE apart (they beat slowly),
//   over a sub an octave down; it swells in while any key is held and dies away slowly after.
//   HORN (the amber key in its title band) switches the horn on and off (lit = on; it fades in 30 ms). Its LAYER (EDIT,
//   then the HORN tab) works on the drone and the horns played from the keys:
//   AMP ENVELOPE (SWELL, RELEASE), FILTER ENVELOPE (attack, decay, sustain, release; it starts with each swell), TUNE
//   (FOG TUNE, DETUNE), TONE (the low-pass: TONE 60 Hz - 8 kHz, RESONANCE, ENV AMOUNT +/-6 octaves), BODY (REED and SUB
//   levels, DRIVE - more rasp, level-matched - and OCTAVE -2 .. +1), PITCH (DROP: each note starts up to 12 semitones
//   high and falls into its pitch over DROP TIME; WOBBLE: a slow vibrato, RATE 0.05 - 8 Hz, DEPTH up to 100 cents),
//   with a picture of the note's pitch.
//   VOCAL MIX: voice against fog horn -> the huge reverb (the house broadcast-reverb engine: REVERB SIZE; its decay
//   and mix set by the presets; a SIZE change glides, so the tail swoops rather than clicks) -> a light tape stage -> output stage (CLIP, ceiling -0.3 dBFS) -> LEVEL
// KEYBOARD (in the FOG HORN section):
//   SPLIT (key + LED): the keyboard splits at SPLIT AT (C1 - C7; the arrows step a semitone, Shift an octave). BELOW and
//   ABOVE each choose VOICE (the singers) or HORN (the fog horn played from the keys at the key's pitch, FOG DETUNE,
//   swell and release as the drone's). While a zone plays the horn, the fixed-pitch drone rests.
//   CHOIR (key + LED): each key in a voice zone gets a choir of SINGERS (1 - 8), each a little off the note, with
//   their own throat and place in the stereo field. Each sings 8 - 9 s, takes a 1 s breath (a soft inhale) and
//   rejoins on a fresh vowel; their breaths are staggered, so the note never drops out. The 16 voices are shared (by the keys and the groups): more
//   keys held = fewer singers each (the earlier keys hand some over); held horns keep theirs. BREATH lamp: a singer
//   breathing. Under the pattern (RUN) the singers speak in rhythm and don't breathe.
//   DRIFT gives every choir singer their own envelope too: attack, decay and release times +/-25 %, sustain +/-8 %
//   (at the standard 50 %; twice that at 100 %, none at 0).
//   ONSET: the consonant every note starts on (and each breath's return, and each pattern step): TA DA BA MA NA KA GA
//   PA LA SA, or MIX (a different one each time); "-" = the soft click. Stops close, burst and (T K P) breathe before the
//   voice; M N hum first; L glides in; S hisses. The formants move from the consonant's place into the vowel.
// PATTERN (RUN lit; it never starts by itself): the held keys speak in rhythm - each step of the pattern is a new
//   syllable (a fresh vowel and a consonant click), an accent louder, a rest silent. Five patterns: GLYPH (an
//   irregular, speech-like 16), PULSE (steady, accents on the beat), TRIPLET (12 steps in threes, at 2/3 the step),
//   BROKEN (a stuttering 16), POLY (3 against 4 over 12, accents where they meet). STACCATO: short, clipped
//   syllables (a quarter of the step) instead of held ones. PATTERN RATE: a note value at REAPER's tempo (locked to
//   its grid while it plays), or with SYNC dark a free rate in Hz. The fog horn keeps sounding under the pattern.
//
// DRIFT (0 - 100 %, 50 % = standard): the formants wander a little, each voice on its own (+/-3 %); the fog horn's
//   detune drifts slowly (+/-30 % of FOG DETUNE); the tape stage flutters (wow and flutter, up to 0.2 ms).
// PRESETS: Default, Heptapod Call, Low Atmospheric Fog, Choppy Staccato Speech, Alien Pulse, Massive Drone Node,
//   Rhythmic Glyphs, Linguistic Tension, Deep Space Rumble, Vocal Stutter, Minimalist Sequence, Dark Horizon, SATB
//   Cathedral, Gated Choir, Bending Horns, Step Chant - level-
//   matched (OUTPUT LEVEL); a preset never starts or stops RUN; every change glides (no clicks).
//   CHOIR in Heptapod Call (bass, 4 singers), Linguistic Tension (alto, 2), Dark Horizon (alto, 3); SPLIT with the
//   horn below and a choir above in Low Atmospheric Fog and Massive Drone Node (split C3, 4 singers; Massive Drone Node's
//   choir tenor) and Deep Space Rumble (split G2, 2 singers).
//   v1.1: Heptapod Call's bass opens slowly (filter envelope); Low Atmospheric Fog stacks bass and tenor (LP 24) over
//   a horn that drops 5 semitones and opens as it swells; Alien Pulse's alto through a band-pass that its envelope
//   flicks; Massive Drone Node adds the bass an octave down over a driven, wobbling horn; Deep Space Rumble's horn an
//   octave down, driven and resonant; Dark Horizon adds a soft soprano and sweeps the alto with its LFO (2 bars).
//   New: SATB Cathedral (all four groups, bass -1 and soprano +1 octave, a choir of 2 each), Gated Choir (tenor and
//   alto chopped by their step sequencers, the alto panning), Bending Horns (every key a horn that falls 12 semitones
//   into its note), Step Chant (the bass's resonant low-pass played by its steps, a soprano drifting on its LFO).
//   v1.1.1: the STEP SEQUENCER in every preset - each preset's groups step their filters (some gate and pan too);
//   Default's bass steps a resonant low-pass (LP 12, 900 Hz) in eighths. Bending Horns sings a gated soprano above C4.
//   Preset changes are click-free: resonance, step and LFO depths glide, a MODE change dips smoothly, the LFO keeps its
//   phase through a RATE change, and the tape stage's flutter depth (DRIFT) glides.
//   Every preset sets each group's pattern (or the first one). A group a preset switches off lets go of its notes.
// GUI: S / M / L / ? (credits, manual link); drag knobs (Shift = fine), wheel, double-click or Ctrl-click = default.
// MIDI: 16 voices, click-free stealing (a 3 ms fade), sustain pedal, pitch bend +/-2 st, all-notes-off (CC 120 / 123);
//   released when the transport stops. MIDI passes through.
// Latency: 0 samples.
//
// STATUS: v1.1.1 - in the Lab (Oct 2026): the SATB groups and their layers (each with a filter LFO and a step sequencer),
//   the fog horn's layer, 16 presets.

import gfx-lab-drift.jsfx-inc
import gfx-lab-output.jsfx-inc
import gfx-lab-uimin.jsfx-inc
import gfx-lab-bverb.jsfx-inc

out_pin:left output
out_pin:right output

